@title Orders Platform Architecture
@subtitle Kestrel Outfitters
@author Commerce Platform
@date Last reviewed 2026-10-01

## Overview

The Orders platform takes web orders, reserves stock and charges cards. It handles about 3,200 orders per hour at peak.

## Architecture diagram

diagram orders dir=LR title="Orders platform"
orders: customers "Customers" user
orders: stripe "Stripe" ext
orders: alb "Application Load Balancer" lb
orders: ordsvc "Orders Service" svc "ECS Fargate, 6 tasks" focus
orders: invsvc "Stock Service" svc "ECS Fargate, 4 tasks"
orders: notifsvc "Notification Service" svc
orders: db "Orders DB" db "RDS PostgreSQL 16" focus
orders: events "Order Events" queue "SQS"
orders: ecr "ECR Registry" store
orders: customers -> alb : HTTPS
orders: alb -> ordsvc : /orders
orders: alb -> invsvc : /inventory
orders: ordsvc -> db : SQL
orders: ordsvc -> events : publish
orders: events --> invsvc : poll
orders: events -> notifsvc : subscribe
orders: ordsvc -> stripe : charge
orders: ecr --> ordsvc : image pull
orders: group vpc "Orders VPC 10.20.0.0/16" alb, ordsvc, invsvc, notifsvc, db
orders: group prod "Prod account" vpc, events
orders: group shared "Shared services account" ecr

## Components

table = Component,Runtime,Purpose; Orders Service,"ECS Fargate, 6 tasks",Accepts orders and charges cards; Stock Service,"ECS Fargate, 4 tasks",Reserves stock; Orders DB,"RDS PostgreSQL 16, db.r6g.xlarge, Multi-AZ",Stores orders; Order Events,"SQS standard queue, 14-day retention",Carries order events to inventory

## Failure modes

!! An Orders DB Multi-AZ failover takes about 60 seconds. During that window order writes fail and the storefront shows a retry banner.
